# THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt records a sha256 of each file it was generated from,
# over the bytes on disk, and third-party-licenses.test.ts recomputes them. A
# checkout that converted line endings would change all nine digests at once and
# leave the notice's own header unparseable — on a Windows runner, where git's
# default core.autocrlf=true does exactly that. `eol=lf` overrides autocrlf, so
# every checkout gets the bytes the digests were taken over.
#
# The rule is repository-wide rather than a list of the generator's inputs: that
# list is computed at generation time (scripts/spdx/*.txt is a glob), so spelling
# it here would create a second place for a new input to be forgotten. Nothing is
# renormalized by adding this — all 381 text files were already stored with LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Marked explicitly rather than left to git's detection. Every file in
# src-tauri/icons/ is generated from app-icon.png and compared byte-for-byte by
# the release workflow, and icon.icns is not byte-reproducible across runs to
# begin with — a heuristic deciding one of them is text would be a defect nobody
# would think to look for here.
*.png -text
*.ico -text
*.icns -text
